sn35.20:1.6 | P: phoṭṭhabbe … | T: “Whoever delights in tactile sensations delights in stress…
sn35.20:1.7 | P: dhamme abhinandati, dukkhaṁ so abhinandati. | T: “Monks, whoever delights in ideas delights in stress.
sn35.20:1.8 | P: Yo dukkhaṁ abhinandati, ‘aparimutto so dukkhasmā’ti vadāmi. | T: Whoever delights in stress is not released from stress, I tell you.
sn35.20:2.1 | P: “Yo ca kho, bhikkhave, rūpe nābhinandati, dukkhaṁ so nābhinandati. | T: “Monks, whoever doesn’t delight in forms doesn’t delight in stress.
sn35.20:2.2 | P: Yo dukkhaṁ nābhinandati, ‘aparimutto so dukkhasmā’ti vadāmi. | T: Whoever doesn’t delight in stress is released from stress, I tell you.
